# Scratchpad. Omarchy's is a special workspace drawn as a Quake console over
# whatever you are on; macOS spaces cannot overlay, so this stays what AeroSpace
# did -- a labelled workspace you toggle in and out of.
#
# Deliberately NOT yabai's own `window --scratchpad`, which is the closer
# analogue but needs the scripting addition. A labelled space works on any
# machine, which matters while the addition's status on macOS 26.6 is unsettled.
#
# Omarchy binds both Super+Grave and Super+S, so both are here. cmd-s costs Save
# everywhere -- macos-app-shortcuts.sh puts it back on ctrl-s. Sending a window
# there is cmd-shift-backtick / cmd-alt-s: cmd-shift-s is the Google Maps
# launcher, not a scratchpad key.
cmd - 0x32         : /opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m query --spaces --space | /opt/homebrew/bin/jq -e '.label == "scratch"' >/dev/null && /opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m space --focus recent || /opt/homebrew/bin/yabai -m space --focus scratch
